    },
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Don’t boast about tomorrow,",
          "for you don’t know what a day might bring."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let another praise you, and not your own mouth —",
          "a stranger, and not your own lips."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A stone is heavy, and sand a burden,",
          "but aggravation from a fool outweighs them both."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Fury is cruel, and anger a flood,",
          "but who can withstand jealousy?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Better an open reprimand",
          "than concealed love."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The wounds of a friend are trustworthy,",
          "but the kisses of an enemy are excessive."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A person who is full tramples on a honeycomb,",
          "but to a hungry person, any bitter thing is sweet."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Anyone wandering from his home",
          "is like a bird wandering from its nest."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Oil and incense bring joy to the heart,",
          "and the sweetness of a friend is better than self-counsel."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Don’t abandon your friend or your father’s friend,",
          "and don’t go to your brother’s house",
          "in your time of calamity;",
          "better a neighbor nearby than a brother far away."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Be wise, my son, and bring my heart joy,",
          "so that I can answer anyone who taunts me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A sensible person sees danger and takes cover;",
          "the inexperienced keep going and are punished."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Take his garment,",
          "for he has put up security for a stranger;",
          "get collateral if it is for foreigners. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If one blesses his neighbor",
          "with a loud voice early in the morning,",
          "it will be counted as a curse to him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "An endless dripping on a rainy day",
          "and a nagging wife are alike;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "the one who controls her controls the wind",
          "and grasps oil with his right hand."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Iron sharpens iron,",
          "and one person sharpens another."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Whoever tends a fig tree will eat its fruit,",
          "and whoever looks after his master will be honored."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "As water reflects the face,",
          "so the heart reflects the person."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Sheol and Abaddon are never satisfied,",
          "and people’s eyes are never satisfied."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "As a crucible refines silver,",
          "and a smelter refines gold,",
          "so a person should refine his praise."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Though you grind a fool",
          "in a mortar with a pestle along with grain,",
          "you will not separate his foolishness from him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Know well the condition of your flock,",
          "and pay attention to your herds,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "for wealth is not forever;",
          "not even a crown lasts for all time."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "When hay is removed and new growth appears",
          "and the grain from the hills is gathered in,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "lambs will provide your clothing,",
          "and goats, the price of a field;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "there will be enough goat’s milk for your food —",
          "food for your household",
          "and nourishment for your female servants."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
